{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useAsyncRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts#L59","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts:59"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A React hook that creates a rate-limited version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncRateLimiter"},{"type":"text","value":" hook,\nproviding a stable, async rate-limited function reference for use in React components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Async rate limiting is a \"hard limit\" approach for async functions: it allows all calls\nuntil the limit is reached, then blocks (rejects) subsequent calls until the window resets.\nUnlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out or collapse calls.\nThis can lead to bursts of rapid executions followed by periods where all calls are blocked."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The async rate limiter supports two types of windows:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All executions within the window count\ntowards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'sliding': A rolling window that allows executions as old ones expire. This provides a more\nconsistent rate of execution over time."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For smoother execution patterns, consider:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useAsyncThrottledCallback: When you want consistent spacing between executions (e.g. UI updates)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useAsyncDebouncedCallback: When you want to collapse rapid calls into a single execution (e.g. search input)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Async rate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits\non async operations, like API rate limits or other scenarios requiring hard caps\non execution frequency."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook provides a simpler API compared to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncRateLimiter"},{"type":"text","value":", making it ideal for basic\nasync rate limiting needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncRateLimiter instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For advanced usage requiring features like:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual cancellation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Access to execution counts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom useCallback dependencies"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncRateLimiter"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactAsyncRateLimiterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Awaited"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReturnType"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">> | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Rate limit async API calls to maximum 5 calls per minute with a sliding window\nconst makeApiCall = useAsyncRateLimitedCallback(\n  async (data: ApiData) => {\n    return fetch('/api/endpoint', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) });\n  },\n  {\n    limit: 5,\n    window: 60000, // 1 minute\n    windowType: 'sliding',\n    onReject: () => {\n      console.warn('API rate limit reached. Please wait before trying again.');\n    }\n  }\n);","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts:59](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts#L59)\n\nA React hook that creates a rate-limited version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncRateLimiter` hook,\nproviding a stable, async rate-limited function reference for use in React components.\n\nAsync rate limiting is a \"hard limit\" approach for async functions: it allows all calls\nuntil the limit is reached, then blocks (rejects) subsequent calls until the window resets.\nUnlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out or collapse calls.\nThis can lead to bursts of rapid executions followed by periods where all calls are blocked.\n\nThe async rate limiter supports two types of windows:\n- 'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All executions within the window count\n  towards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period.\n- 'sliding': A rolling window that allows executions as old ones expire. This provides a more\n  consistent rate of execution over time.\n\nFor smoother execution patterns, consider:\n- useAsyncThrottledCallback: When you want consistent spacing between executions (e.g. UI updates)\n- useAsyncDebouncedCallback: When you want to collapse rapid calls into a single execution (e.g. search input)\n\nAsync rate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits\non async operations, like API rate limits or other scenarios requiring hard caps\non execution frequency.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncRateLimiter`, making it ideal for basic\nasync rate limiting needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncRateLimiter instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncRateLimiter` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactAsyncRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/ReactAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Rate limit async API calls to maximum 5 calls per minute with a sliding window\nconst makeApiCall = useAsyncRateLimitedCallback(\n  async (data: ApiData) => {\n    return fetch('/api/endpoint', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) });\n  },\n  {\n    limit: 5,\n    window: 60000, // 1 minute\n    windowType: 'sliding',\n    onReject: () => {\n      console.warn('API rate limit reached. Please wait before trying again.');\n    }\n  }\n);\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useAsyncRateLimitedCallback\ntitle: useAsyncRateLimitedCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncRateLimitedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts:59](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/async-rate-limiter/useAsyncRateLimitedCallback.ts#L59)\n\nA React hook that creates a rate-limited version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncRateLimiter` hook,\nproviding a stable, async rate-limited function reference for use in React components.\n\nAsync rate limiting is a \"hard limit\" approach for async functions: it allows all calls\nuntil the limit is reached, then blocks (rejects) subsequent calls until the window resets.\nUnlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out or collapse calls.\nThis can lead to bursts of rapid executions followed by periods where all calls are blocked.\n\nThe async rate limiter supports two types of windows:\n- 'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All executions within the window count\n  towards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period.\n- 'sliding': A rolling window that allows executions as old ones expire. This provides a more\n  consistent rate of execution over time.\n\nFor smoother execution patterns, consider:\n- useAsyncThrottledCallback: When you want consistent spacing between executions (e.g. UI updates)\n- useAsyncDebouncedCallback: When you want to collapse rapid calls into a single execution (e.g. search input)\n\nAsync rate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits\non async operations, like API rate limits or other scenarios requiring hard caps\non execution frequency.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncRateLimiter`, making it ideal for basic\nasync rate limiting needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncRateLimiter instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncRateLimiter` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactAsyncRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/ReactAsyncRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Rate limit async API calls to maximum 5 calls per minute with a sliding window\nconst makeApiCall = useAsyncRateLimitedCallback(\n  async (data: ApiData) => {\n    return fetch('/api/endpoint', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) });\n  },\n  {\n    limit: 5,\n    window: 60000, // 1 minute\n    windowType: 'sliding',\n    onReject: () => {\n      console.warn('API rate limit reached. Please wait before trying again.');\n    }\n  }\n);\n```\n"}
